设$x = \alpha + \beta$且$y = i (\alpha - 2 \beta)$。那么$\alpha - 2 \beta = \frac{y}{i} = -yi$。解出$\alpha$和$\beta$，我们得到\begin{align*}\alpha &= \frac{2}{3} x - \frac{y}{3} i, \\\beta &= \frac{1}{3} x + \frac{y}{3} i。\end{align*}由于$x$和$y$是实数，且$\beta = 3 + 2i,$ 所以$x = 9$且$y = 6$。那么$\alpha = \boxed{6 - 2i}$。答案是$6-2i$。"}

